> > On 2004-09-09, Eva Myers <erm1001@cam.ac.uk> wrote:
> > 
> >> Another possible problem: can you prove that it would be absolutely
> >> impossible for the fire giants ever to kill you?
> > 
> > (assume that you have reflection and all the basic resistances)
> > 
> > Let us assume 25 str [you are a valk, so surely you went with
> > GoP], 18 dex, 14 luck and +7 Mjolnir.  Fire giants have a default AC of
> > 4, meaning you need to roll less than 33 on a 20 sided die to hit them-
> > even if they improve their AC by 12 from putting something on, you still have
> > a 100% chance of hitting them.  You then do at least 9 damage [7 +d4 + d24],
> > although on average, you will do more like 22.  If we go with the 9 damage,
> > and assume a level of say 13 [base level for them is 9- I know it gets
> > adjusted up, but dont feel like checking how much]- they would have at most
> > 13*8=104 HP, which would then take 12 turns to kill.  Fire giants do 2 d 10
> > weapon damage- so let us assume they magically end up with a +7 dwarvish
> > mattock, making for 2 d 10 + d 12 + 7 damage, and that they max that out
> > each time, resulting in 20+12+7=39 damage.  This ignores the fact that
> > you probably have an AC around -60 at this point [being an extinctionist and
> > all] and so they hit you about 25% of the time, as well as the fact
> > that you should be very fast and get more actions.  So they can max out at
> > 468 HP before you can kill them, in the worst imaginable case.  An
> > extinctionist would have way more than this easily, and hey- you can always
> > engrave or something if it poses a problem. 
> 
> None of that matters.
> 
> All that matters is that they have a non-zero chance of doing you in.
> Given infinitely many tries, they're statistically certain to kill you.
> 
> One saving possibility for this threat is potions of healing
> and the associated hit point gain.  If your hit points rise at a steady
> (average) rate then your risk of death will decline exponentially,
> yielding a finite non-zero chance of indefinite survival.

Where are you going to obtain an infinite supply of potions of
healing?  I was thinking that if neither fire giants nor fire ants
could get past your AC, that would keep you safe.  If the maximum
damage they could do in a single round was less than or equal to your
minimum healing rate per round, that would also be enough.  Not having
checked the source or spoilers in detail, I don't know whether this is
possible.

Healing spells could be a big help by boosting that minimum healing
rate.  Standing on a scroll of scare monster could also help, although
you'd have to leave it in order to eat.
Eva.

